Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(pkg): make the preinstall guard safe for consumers

The published package is uninstallable. `preinstall` runs
`node scripts/check-npm-version.mjs`, but `files` is ["dist", "NOTICE.md"], so
scripts/ is never shipped. npm runs a dependency's preinstall, so every consumer
install dies with MODULE_NOT_FOUND. Reproduced against 0.1.1 from the registry in
a clean project.

Ships the script and makes the guard exit early when it detects it is running
from inside a node_modules tree: the npm-10 lockfile hazard it guards
(npm/cli#4828) is about developing this repo, and a consumer on npm 10 is
unaffected.

--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@
   },
   "files": [
     "dist",
+    "scripts/check-npm-version.mjs",
     "NOTICE.md"
   ],
   "scripts": {
--- a/scripts/check-npm-version.mjs
+++ b/scripts/check-npm-version.mjs
@@ -15,6 +15,18 @@
 // npm exposes its own version to lifecycle scripts via the user-agent env var,
 // e.g. "npm/11.18.0 node/v22.14.0 darwin arm64". If it is absent (script run
 // outside an npm lifecycle) we cannot tell, so we do not block.
+// The hook is `preinstall`, which npm also runs for this package when it is
+// installed as somebody else's DEPENDENCY. The lockfile concern is purely about
+// developing THIS repo, and a consumer on npm 10 is unaffected, so bail out as
+// soon as we can tell we are running from inside a node_modules tree. (Without
+// this the guard is actively harmful: `files` does not ship scripts/, so a
+// consumer's install dies with MODULE_NOT_FOUND before npm ever reaches us.)
+import { fileURLToPath } from "node:url";
+
+if (fileURLToPath(import.meta.url).split(/[\\/]/).includes("node_modules")) {
+  process.exit(0);
+}
+
 const ua = process.env.npm_config_user_agent ?? "";
 const match = ua.match(/\bnpm\/(\d+)\./);
 
